OL,4,CMinisters ask public for views on      
OL,5,Cchanging age of consent                
OL,6,GThe government is inviting the public  
OL,7,Gto share its views as ministers        
OL,8,Gconsider whether or not to stagger the 
OL,9,Gage of consent.                        
OL,11,FCurrently adults of any age are        
OL,12,Flegally able to have sex with 16 and   
OL,13,F17-year-olds, however some campaigners 
OL,14,Fhave argued that different limits      
OL,15,Fshould apply, depending on the age gap 
OL,16,Fbetween the people involved.           
OL,18,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham said he    
OL,19,Fwanted survivors, parents, young       
OL,20,Fpeople, victim support services and    
OL,21,Fthe wider public to "to share their    
OL,22,Fexperiences and inform this process".  
